# Tester harness CLIs

## Permission before `--save-result`

Do not run artifact-writing harness CLIs unless the user asked in this chat, a fresh run is required for an explicit request, or you are debugging the harness itself.

Ask first before:

- `./tester_v1_calibrate.py --save-result` (three calibration probes via in-process runs with `--save-result --quiet`; JSON under `tester-v1/results/{model}/{variant}/`; session file under `tester-v1/results/{model}/calibration-sessions/`)
- `./tester_v1_run_test.py --save-result` (JSON under `tester-v1/results/{model}/{variant}/`)

Run these from the repo root. Probe runs without `--save-result` are stdout-only and need no ask.

## Prefer existing local output

`tester-v1/results/` is gitignored. For docs, comparisons, or VRAM/context answers:

1. Use metrics already in repo README or other docs.
2. Else read newest `*.json` under `tester-v1/results/{model}/{variant}/`, or `calibration-sessions/{session_id}.json` for saved calibration.
3. Recompute from those files when needed (`idle_vram_mb`, calibration math).
4. Suggest or run a new harness only if local data is missing, stale, or the user wants a new run.

## Do not use calibration-tests as config_dir

Do not pass `tester-v1/calibration-tests/` (or a variant under it) to `tester_v1_run_test.py`. Pass `models/{model}/` and select a probe or sandbox with `--variant` (default `hello-world-baseline`). Calibration loads probes from `calibration-tests/` internally; pass `models/{model}/` only. See `calibration-tests.mdc`.
